# 3. NON-NEGOTIABLE PRODUCT RULES

These rules must never be violated:

1. Never silently delete completed transactions.
2. Never silently modify posted sales, purchases, payments, or financial records.
3. Never change stock without a traceable stock movement.
4. Never permit negative inventory unless explicitly approved as a future configurable feature. For the initial version, negative stock is prohibited.
5. Never sell expired stock through the normal sales workflow.
6. Never use current medicine cost to calculate the profit of historical sales.
7. Never assume medicine packaging quantities.
8. Never assume every strip contains the same number of tablets.
9. Never assume every box contains the same number of strips.
10. Never assume all medicines use the same unit conversion rules.
11. Never hardcode Box → Strip → Tablet conversion.
12. Never retroactively change historical stock or transactions when unit conversions are edited.
13. Never automatically return customer-returned medicine to sellable stock without inspection and an explicit disposition.
14. Never allow completed financial transactions to be deleted.
15. Never overwrite the customer's database during software updates.
16. Never treat an unverified backup as a successful backup.
17. Never place the licensing private key inside the customer software.
18. Never make customer data inaccessible because a license expires.
19. Never enforce permissions only through frontend/UI hiding.
20. Never perform critical transaction operations outside atomic database transactions.

