# 17. CASH SESSION MANAGEMENT

Support manual cash opening and closing.

Cash session:

Open → Closed

Fields:

- Session ID
- Opening date/time
- Opening user
- Opening cash
- Closing date/time
- Closing user
- Expected cash
- Actual cash
- Cash variance
- Notes
- Status

## Expected cash calculation

Expected cash:

Opening Cash  
+ Cash Received  
− Cash Paid  
+/- Cash Adjustments

## Closing

Actual cash must be physically counted and manually entered.

Variance:

Actual Cash − Expected Cash

When variance exists:

- Record variance.
- Require reason.
- Generate a cash adjustment movement.
- Preserve the original expected balance.
- Preserve the actual counted amount.
- Preserve the user and timestamp.

Do not silently correct the cash ledger.

Forgotten sessions must not be overwritten.

Admin may force-close a session with a mandatory reason and audit trail.

